.nh
.TH "PB-SEND-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-send-list - List file transfers


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb send list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List outgoing transfers to one machine. --on is required: name the machine the
files were sent to. Filter with --q (file name or transfer ID), --state and --session; page
with --limit (default 50) and --offset. Use a listed transfer ID with status or cancel. For
sends to this computer the history is read from the local Inbox.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=50
	maximum transfers to return

.PP
\fB--offset\fP=0
	continue at a transfer history offset

.PP
\fB--on\fP=""
	machine the files were sent to, by name or ID (required)

.PP
\fB--q\fP=""
	filter by file basename or transfer ID

.PP
\fB--session\fP=""
	terminal session ID for destination context

.PP
\fB--state\fP=""
	filter by transfer state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb send list --on laptop
  pb send list --on laptop --state failed --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-send(1)\fP
